// Dark Skies DLC

TIFactionTemplate.CampaignStart.ResistCouncil.2003=Greetings, {0}. I am pleased to report the council has appointed you leader of {1}. I am {2}, your chief of staff.<br/><br/>We represent a small group who believes the alien crash-landing {3} and disappearance may signify a potential threat. We intend to build an international organization capable of investigating and, if necessary, combating any danger aliens may pose.<br/><br/><h>I recommend we send a councilor to investigate the crash site in the {4} region as soon as possible. Our other councilors may be best used in trying to gain influence in nations that may be able to contribute resources to our cause.</h><br/><br/>You may review our objectives at any time by clicking our faction symbol in the top-left corner of your screen. // rank, council name, leader name

TIFactionTemplate.leader.description.ResistCouncil.2003=Captain, British Army Intelligence Corps, ret. 1989; Case Officer, undisclosed location, Secret Intelligence Service, 1989-1990; SIS liaison to The Trevi Group, 1991-1992; Chief of Station, Lagos, 1992-1995; Chief of Station, Islamabad, 1995-1997; Deputy Chief of African Affairs, 1997-1998; Senior adviser to insurgent group, location undisclosed, 1999-present.
TIFactionTemplate.leader.description.DestroyCouncil.2003=Enlisted Paratrooper in Falklands War, awarded for bravery at Battle of Mount Longdon in 1982. Trained U.S. Army School of the Americas, 1976. Served as a line officer or adviser with various anti-separatist special operations units and militias in Venezuela, Panama, and Peru, in the 1980s. Worked in Pentagon’s Latin America policy arm in 1990s. In 1995, briefly imprisoned in Buenos Aires on war crimes charges stemming from alleged activities during Operation Condor in the early 1980s; acquitted in 1996.
TIFactionTemplate.leader.description.ExploitCouncil.2003=Various positions with arms manufacturer Western Armories, 1987-present, including chairman of the board since 1997. Minority ownership stake in DWKY Industries, which has diamond mining partnerships with the governments of Botswana and Namibia. He is occasionally criticized in activist media for labor practices of his various interests, but no formal investigations are known to have taken place.
TIFactionTemplate.leader.description.EscapeCouncil.2003=Master of Physics and Philosophy, Oxford University, 1991; Lead investor, Al Zaabi Satellite Communications. Noted financial supporter of several space enthusiast organizations and publications.
TIFactionTemplate.leader.description.SubmitCouncil.2003=Attended Southwestern Baptist Theological Seminary, Fort Worth, Texas, departed 1995  without degree. Charged with incitement and transporting controlled substances related to the mass suicide of members of the Eternal Source cult in Arizona in 1997; charges were later dropped. Worked as content manager for a collection of California-based New Age web sites predicting alien arrival in the coming decades, 1998-present, during which time she became a popular public speaker and self-help guru.
TIFactionTemplate.leader.description.AppeaseCouncil.2003=B.A. in Political Science, University of Chennai, 1968, where he was a civil rights activist. Shot by police during a protest in Muzaffarnagar, Uttar Pradesh, in 1967. Resided in Vancouver, Canada, 1967-1973. Worked as civilian monitor and ombudsman for U.N. Peacekeeping operations in various locations, including Baluchistan, El Salvador, and Moldova, 1973-1993. Master of Laws with a focus on international human rights law, Concordia University, 1977. Testified at war crimes tribunals as well as during prosecutions of peacekeepers who committed serious offenses during missions. Since 1993, he has served as an adviser to various human rights and peace organizations.
TIFactionTemplate.leader.description.CooperateCouncil.2003=B.S., Astronautical Engineering; Tsinghua University, 1983; M.S. and PhD, Chemistry, Massachusetts Institute of Technology, 1987; PhD, Public Management, Tsinghua University, 1990; Professor of Science and Technology Policy and Management, Xi'an Jiaotong University, 1991-present; Director, Department of Higher Education, Ministry of Education, 1997–2000